#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
# g16-testd: one root helper per G16 test session (#277). EXPERIMENTAL, G16 only.
#
#   g16-testd session start [--hours H] [--module NAME=SHA256]...
#                                  open a session: one polkit dialog starts the root
#                                  daemon as a transient system unit, for H hours
#                                  (4, at most 12); NAME=SHA256 are the only module
#                                  builds module-swap may load in this session
#   g16-testd session stop         put everything back (knobs, modules, drop-ins,
#                                  traces, frozen scopes) and end the session
#   g16-testd session status       expiry and what is changed right now
#   g16-testd available            exit 0 when a session is open for this user
#   g16-testd list                 the allowlists (knobs, events, kprobes, drop-ins)
#   g16-testd cleanup              root, from the package's removal: stop an open
#                                  session and put back all it left, drop-ins included
#   g16-testd call METHOD ARG... --reason TEXT
#                                  one root step; METHOD is one of
#     ec-read OFFSET LEN                  EC RAM bytes through ec_sys, read-only
#     trace-start NAME EVENTS [KPROBES] [BUFFER_KB]
#                                         a private tracefs instance; EVENTS and KPROBES
#                                         are comma lists from the allowlists ("-": none)
#     trace-stop NAME                     stop it; the trace is handed to you (an open
#                                         file: the helper keeps no copy), written to
#                                         $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omarchy-asus-g16-testd/NAME.trace,
#                                         and the instance and its kprobes are removed
#     knob-set KNOB VALUE / knob-restore KNOB
#     module-swap NAME PATH / module-restore NAME
#     boot-dropin NAME on|off             prints the resulting kernel command lines
#     freeze SCOPE [SECONDS] / thaw SCOPE user app scopes only; thawed after SECONDS
#                                         (300, at most 1800) whatever happens
#
# The daemon runs only fixed operations on fixed allowlists; nothing a caller sends is
# run as a command. It answers only the user who opened the session (the socket is
# theirs, mode 0600, and every connection's peer uid is checked). Every change is
# recorded under /var/lib/omarchy-asus-g16-testd before it is made, and put back on
# `session stop`, at expiry, when the daemon is stopped, and at the next start after a
# crash. Boot drop-ins outlive a reboot on purpose (a boot A/B needs one): they go on
# `session stop`, at expiry, or with `boot-dropin NAME off`. Every call is logged to the
# journal with the caller's uid and pid and the reason.
#
# Test mode keeps the laptop awake: `session start` records Omarchy's stay-awake state
# (omarchy-toggle-idle status) and turns it on, so no idle dim, lock or suspend cuts
# into an unattended A/B. The end of the session (stop, expiry, the unit stopping, or
# the next start after a crash) runs allow-idle only if stay-awake was off before.
#
# Exit status: 0 done, 1 refused or failed, 2 bad usage, 3 no session open.
